    <li class="nav-dd"><a href="#">WQI</a><div class="dd-menu"><a href="/w6swqi">Simple WQI</a><a href="/w4nsfwqi">NSF-WQI</a><a href="/w5wawqi">WA-WQI</a><a href="/w1ccmewqi">CCME-WQI</a></div></li>
    <li><a href="/treatment">Treatment</a></li><li><a href="/AQI">AQI</a></li><li><a href="/parameters" style="color:var(--accent)">Parameters</a></li><li><a href="/information">Data Info</a></li>
  </ul>
  <button class="nav-toggle" onclick="document.getElementById('navLinks').classList.toggle('open')"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button>
</nav>

<div class="param-page">
  <div class="param-container">
    <a href="/parameters" class="btn btn-ghost" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">← Back to Parameters Directory</a>

    <div class="param-card fu">
      <span class="badge badge-purple">Biological / Chemical Parameter</span>
      <h1 style="font-size:2.2rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--white);margin-top:0.5rem">Biochemical Oxygen Demand (BOD)</h1>
      
      <div class="param-meta">
        <div class="meta-box"><div class="meta-lbl">Standard Test</div><div class="meta-val">BOD₅ (20°C, 5 Days)</div></div>
        <div class="meta-box"><div class="meta-lbl">Pristine River</div><div class="meta-val">&lt; 1 mg/L</div></div>
        <div class="meta-box"><div class="meta-lbl">Raw Sewage</div><div class="meta-val">200 - 600 mg/L</div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="content-sec">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>Biochemical Oxygen Demand (BOD) represents the amount of dissolved oxygen consumed by aerobic microorganisms to decompose organic material in water over a specified incubation period (typically 5 days at 20°C).</p>
        
        <h2>Environmental Significance</h2>
        <p>A higher BOD level indicates a greater amount of organic matter present in the water body. As microorganisms rapidly decompose organic waste (from municipal sewage, agricultural runoff, or industrial effluents), available dissolved oxygen drops rapidly, suffocating fish and aquatic organisms.</p>
        
        <h2>Common Pollution Sources</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Domestic and municipal sewage discharges</li>
          <li>Food processing plant and brewery effluents</li>
          <li>Agricultural runoff containing livestock manure</li>
          <li>Pulp and paper mill waste</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--r);padding:1.5rem;margin-top:2rem">
        <h3 style="color:var(--accent);font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem">🧪 Testing & Measurement</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted)">BOD₅ is measured by calculating the difference between initial dissolved oxygen and dissolved oxygen remaining after 5 days of sealed dark incubation at 20°C in standard BOD bottles.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

